%erg v1
Title: Drop post-talk and post-conference from hardcoded tag vocabulary
Created: 2026-05-11
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-11T14:30Z claude open — surfaced during audit lint review of ergspecv1.go

--- body ---
## Problem

The v1 tag vocabulary hardcodes four values: needs-human, deferred,
post-talk, post-conference. The first two are generic workflow states.
The last two are personal calendar labels that leaked into a reusable
spec. No live ticket has ever used post-talk or post-conference.

Affected code:
- ergspecv1.go: validTagValues map
- ready.go: skipReadyTags map (duplicate of validTagValues)
- validate_test.go: test fixtures referencing post-talk/post-conference

## Options

A. Drop post-talk and post-conference from the closed set. Keep
   needs-human and deferred. Simplest fix, nothing breaks in practice.

B. Make the tag vocabulary user-configurable (e.g. .erg-tags file or
   env var). Solves the root cause — the spec should not hardcode
   workflow-specific labels. More work.

C. Do A now, B later if needed.

## Origin

Ticket 0015 designed Tags as a closed value set with the rationale that
unknown values fail validation rather than parsing silently. That
rationale holds for A — the set just gets smaller.
